    "summary": "Man&#039;s gown (tobe, boubou, riga), composed of 52 hand-woven narrow strips of hand-spun cotton, hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The trunk is assembled vertically, the sleeves horizontally. The neck opening, shoulders and back are hand-embroidered in brown thread in the &#039;two knives&#039; pattern using satin and buttonhole eyelet stitch. The openings are all hemmed.",
